---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Aurora from '../components/Aurora.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Manifesto — Maxxtopia"
  description="Why Maxxtopia exists. The principles behind the suite."
>
  <article class="relative">
    <Aurora intensity="low" />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-grid opacity-30"></div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 sm:px-8 pt-24 pb-12">
      <p class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--color-magenta)] font-mono reveal reveal-1">
        Manifesto · v0.1
      </p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-2 mt-4 text-[44px] sm:text-[68px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-[1] gradient-text">
        We're tired of <span class="serif-accent gradient-suite">bad gaming software.</span>
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 sm:px-8 pb-32">
      <div class="space-y-7 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.78] text-[var(--color-text-mid)]">
        <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
          The tools competitive gamers actually use weren't built by anyone competitive.
          They were built by Discord scripters who slapped a paywall on a registry batch file,
          by Electron studios shipping 200 MB of Chromium for a settings panel,
          by analytics-funded SaaS that treats your inputs as inventory.
        </p>

        <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
          Maxxtopia is a refusal to accept that.
          We think gaming utilities should be designed with the care Apple gives a music app.
          That a tuner should cite its sources. That a Discord client should idle at 0% CPU.
          That a clip tool should measure what actually goes viral, not just spike on volume.
          That nothing in your gaming stack should call home unless you tell it to.
        </p>

        <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll text-[var(--color-text)] text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] pt-6 leading-tight">
          Principles
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-5">
          {[
            { t: 'Sourced, not guessed.', b: "Every tweak we ship traces to Microsoft Learn, a vendor doc, or a verified community source. If it can't be cited, it doesn't ship. Placebo tweaks erode trust — we cut ten of them in v0.1.32." },
            { t: 'Native or nothing.', b: 'The tuner is 3.6 MB. The Discord client is 288 MB at idle versus 1041 MB on stock. Bundle size is a moral position.' },
            { t: 'Reversible by default.', b: 'Every change is snapshot-backed. Every preset is undoable. One-click restore. Software you can experiment with because the door is never locked.' },
            { t: 'No telemetry. Ever.', b: "We don't analytics you. We don't error-log you. We don't “help us improve our product” you. Gaming software has a long history of betraying that trust. We won't." },
            { t: "Measure, don't just modify.", b: "Every tuner applies tweaks. Maxxtopia's ships live DPC graphs, latency probes, and PCIe diagnostics so you can verify the change worked. Trust, then verify." },
          ].map((p) => (
            <div class="reveal-on-scroll relative pl-6">
              <span class="absolute left-0 top-1.5 bottom-1.5 w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-[var(--color-magenta)] via-[var(--color-cyan)] to-transparent"></span>
              <h3 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[19px] font-semibold mb-2 tracking-[-0.01em]">{p.t}</h3>
              <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7] text-[var(--color-text-mid)]">{p.b}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll text-[var(--color-text)] text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] pt-6 leading-tight">
          The suite
        </h2>

        <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
          Optimizationmaxxing tunes your PC.
          Discordmaxxer tunes your comms.
          Clipmaxxer cuts your VODs.
          Dropmaxxer picks your spots.
          Aimmaxxer drills your gap.
          Viewmaxxing handles your stream.
          Editmaxxing assists your edits.
        </p>

        <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
          Different surfaces. <span class="serif-accent text-[var(--color-text)]">Same standard.</span>
          Built by a single player for the players who care about the millisecond.
        </p>

        <p class="reveal-on-scroll pt-6">
          <span class="slogan">made by diggy</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal-on-scroll mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-[var(--color-line)]">
        <a href="/#suite" class="btn-primary">
          Browse the suite
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
